      <div class="lead">
        <p>Water-based aerosol systems continue to gain widespread adoption in industrial cleaners, household care, automotive maintenance products, agricultural inputs, and cosmetic sprays. They reduce volatile organic compounds (VOCs), improve environmental compliance, and allow safer handling. However, the presence of water inside a sealed, pressurized metal container changes the corrosion environment dramatically. Water functions as an electrolyte, transports ions, solvates gases, interacts with headspace vapors, and destabilizes protective oxide layers on metal surfaces.</p>
      </div>

